# /opt/inflect/.env.scanner: the harness scanner's credentials, and nothing else.
#
# Root-owned, mode 0600. Compose reads it into the one container's environment;
# it is never mounted. A value never goes into config.json, which the scanner
# refuses if it holds one. deploy/harness-scanner/config.pilot.example.json
# names each line below.
#
# Quoting is Compose's dotenv: inside "double quotes" a \n becomes a newline;
# inside 'single quotes' nothing is expanded.
#
# The Ed25519 signing key, PKCS#8 PEM, double-quoted with \n for each line
# break. Its public half is registered against the scanner in Inflect.
SCANNER_SIGNING_KEY=
# An Inflect API key bound to the scanner agent, holding admin:harness_ingest
# and mcp:read and nothing else. It posts the report, reads the register, and
# lists /api/mcp's tools. The scanner agent is granted get_harness_register.
INFLECT_INGEST_KEY=
# The secret of an Entra application holding Application.Read.All, and nothing
# that writes.
ENTRA_CLIENT_SECRET=
# A fine-grained GitHub token for the one repository, holding Contents: read and
# Secrets: read and nothing else.
GITHUB_READ_TOKEN=
# The JSON key of a GCP service account holding roles/iam.serviceAccountViewer
# on the one project and no other role, on one line and single-quoted, so the
# \n escapes inside its private_key stay as JSON wrote them.
GCP_SCANNER_KEY=
